<.shell title="Map" current={:map}>
  <h1>Map</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    A plain Mapbox map with a dot per activity in its kind's colour.
  </p>

  <div style="max-width: 720px">
    <.activity_map
      :if={chart_map()}
      id="sample-map"
      map={chart_map()}
      label="Map of sample activities"
    >
      <ul class="chart-legend" style="flex-direction: column; margin: 0">
        <li><i class="chart-key is-dot series-incident"></i>6 incidents</li>
        <li><i class="chart-key is-dot series-exercise"></i>3 exercises</li>
        <li><i class="chart-key is-dot series-event"></i>1 event</li>
      </ul>
    </.activity_map>
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      It draws Mapbox's <code>outdoors-v12</code> in light mode and <code>dark-v11</code> in dark
      mode, so a map never glares on a dark page.
    </li>
    <li>
      Places are our dots in the kind's colour, not Mapbox pins. One place is one dot.
    </li>
    <li>Without a Mapbox token the dots sit on a plain panel, and the page still works.</li>
    <li>
      Dots have a 2px ring so they read where they overlap, and incidents sit on top. Hover a dot for the activity.
    </li>
    <li>The activity page uses the same map with one dot.</li>
    <li>
      Points more than 150 km from the team's base are left off, so one activity with a wrong
      place in D4H does not zoom the map out to the whole province.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    Every map is <code>&lt;.activity_map&gt;</code>
    from <code>Web.Components.ActivityMap</code>, never a bare Mapbox image.
  </p>
</.shell>
